cut - select fields or byte columns from text

SYNOPSIS
    cut -c list [file ...]
    cut [-s] [-d delimiter] -f list [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Use a comma-separated list of numbers or ranges, starting at 1.
    Fields use tabs by default. With -s, skip lines without the delimiter.
    A file named - reads standard input.

EXAMPLES
    cut -d : -f 1,3 data

SEE ALSO
    paste(1), grep(1)
